@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Example resource property automaton

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #495057
}

state "not yet allocated" as Untracked #F1F3F5
state "open\n(non-accepting)" as Open #FFF3BF
state "closed\n(accepting)" as Closed #D3F9D8
state "error\n(absorbing)" as Error #FFE3E3

[*] --> Untracked
Untracked --> Open : open / allocate object
Open --> Open : use
Open --> Closed : close
Open --> Error : every other property event
Closed --> Error : use or close
Error --> Error : every property event
Closed --> [*] : acceptable function exit

note right of Untracked
  No fact exists before the allocation site.
  Each allocation call creates a distinct object.
end note

note right of Error
  A missing ordinary transition is forbidden.
  The designated error state is absorbing,
  so one path does not emit duplicate follow-on findings.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#F1F3F5>| no tracked object yet |
|<#FFF3BF>| live resource state |
|<#D3F9D8>| acceptable terminal state |
|<#FFE3E3>| forbidden-transition state |
endlegend
@enduml
